<title>TAJIKISTAN: Airport in Tajik capital re-starts operations.</title>
<headline>Airport in Tajik capital re-starts operations.</headline>
<dateline>DUSHANBE 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The main airport in the Tajik capital Dushanbe re-started operations on Friday following $4 million worth of repairs.</p>
<p>The head of Tajikistan's state-owned airline, Mirzo Mastangulov, said the $4 million costs were paid for by the Dutch government through the European Bank of Reconstruction and Development.</p>
<p>Aircraft of up to 300 tonnes could now land at the airport, Mastangulov said. Earlier, the airport's capacity was limited to aircraft weighing up to 130 tonnes.</p>
<p>He also said Tajikistan's national carrier would begin regular flights from Dushanbe to destinations in Japan, Malaysia, Singapore and the United States in 1997.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
